Description: virgl video: NV12/P010-only codec surfaces, readback of decoded frames, 2D_ARRAY views for the compositor (local, not upstream)
 For VA-API through virgl to a Proxmox host (virglrenderer + radeonsi), see
 https://github.com/fvlaicu/pve-virgl-build (docs/DESIGN.md, "The problem").
 .
 1. virgl_is_video_format_supported: for decode and encode entrypoints, offer only
    NV12 and P010. virglrenderer allocates the host VA surface from the chroma
    format alone (YUV420 -> NV12, YUV420_10 -> P010) and pairs guest and host
    planes by index, so a guest buffer in I420/YV12 lost its V plane. ffmpeg
    picks I420 for 8-bit decoding when offered (vaapi_decode_find_best_format).
    radeonsi on bare metal offers only NV12/P010 too.
 2. virgl_video_end_frame: mark a decode target's plane resources dirty. The host
    writes the decoded picture into them at END_FRAME; without this the guest
    considers them clean and vaGetImage/hwdownload returned the guest's
    never-written copy (flat frames).
 3. Component sampler views of video buffers get target 2D_ARRAY. The vl
    compositor (scale_vaapi etc.; virgl has no video engine for it) samples them
    with TGSI_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY shaders while progressive buffers are 2D textures;
    on the virgl host that sampler2DArray read zeros (scaled frames black). With
    a 2D_ARRAY view the host makes a matching GL texture view.
Author: local virgl build <root@localhost>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-16
